A||||1||afRaceR||Question about alternator||||1||
Z||000000||afRaceR||11-28-2000||10:24 PM||||Ok, here's another new problem my car just got. My battery light has started to just barely come on at idle. I checked the alternator and its putting out 14.5V at idle. So what's the deal? My alternotor is fine, so why is the light coming on?||||reg||1
Z||000001||PlasticWrapd||11-29-2000||05:16 AM||||Couls be a number of things...  first, remove all of the wires and clean the connection points.  If they are corroded, you can prevent this in the future with a product called NoAlOx ( pronounced "no-locks").  You can get it at just about any electrical supply store.  It prevents corrosion at electrical connections.  Check the ground, and if necessary, run a sperate ground wire from the alternator to the battery or chassis.  Finally, get a volt meter and set it to read AC (alternating current).  Check the alternator output.  If you get a reading above 6 volts, then the diodes in the alternator are failing.  This would be the most likely cause, but cleaning the terminals will sometimes fix the problem||||reg||1
